.TH OPENCRYPTOKI 7 "August 2026" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "openCryptoki"
.SH NAME
openCryptoki \- A PKCS#11 implementation.

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBopenCryptoki\fP is an implementation of the PKCS#11 API standard. It
provides an interface to the functions of underlying cryptographic
tokens, which may be implemented via software or hardware. The PKCS#11
specification is maintained by OASIS. More information on PKCS#11
can be found on the OASIS website: https://www.oasis-open.org/committees/pkcs11/

openCryptoki implements PKCS#11 version 3.0 and partially versions 3.1
and 3.2.

.SS "Supported Platforms"
openCryptoki runs on Linux on IBM Z (s390x), Linux on IBM Power (ppc64le),
Linux on x86-64 (x86_64), Linux on ARM (aarch64), and AIX. Not all token
backends are available on every platform; see the individual token
descriptions below.

.SS "Token Backends"
The following token backends are available:
.TP
.B Software token (swtok)
A pure-software token using OpenSSL. Available on all supported platforms.
.TP
.B ICA token (icatok)
A token using the IBM libica library for hardware-accelerated cryptography.
Only available on Linux on IBM Z (s390x).
.TP
.B CCA token (ccatok)
A token using the IBM Common Cryptographic Architecture (CCA) library
with IBM Crypto Express adapters. Available on Linux on IBM Z (s390x),
Linux on IBM Power (ppc64le), Linux on x86-64, and AIX.
.TP
.B EP11 token (ep11tok)
A token using IBM Crypto Express adapters configured with Enterprise
PKCS#11 (EP11) firmware. Only available on Linux on IBM Z (s390x).
.TP
.B ICSF token (icsftok)
A token using the z/OS Integrated Cryptographic Service Facility (ICSF)
via LDAP, for remote cryptographic operations on IBM Z. Available on
Linux; not supported on AIX.
.TP
.B TPM token (tpmtok, deprecated)
A token using a Trusted Platform Module (TPM 1.2 only). Available on
Linux platforms where the TrouSerS stack is present. This token is
deprecated and will be removed in a future release.

To use openCryptoki, run the \fIpkcsslotd\fP daemon. The daemon will
read the \fIopencryptoki.conf\fP file to collect information about the
tokens and their slots.

Use the \fIpkcsconf\fP utility to further configure openCryptoki once the
daemon is running. The \fIp11sak\fP tool can be used to manage keys and
certificates in a token repository. Mechanism usage statistics can be
collected and displayed using the \fIpkcsstats\fP tool. Algorithm and
key-strength policies can be configured via \fIpolicy.conf\fP and
\fIstrength.conf\fP.

.SH "SECURITY NOTE"
All non-root users that require access to PKCS#11 tokens using openCryptoki
must be assigned to the \fI@pkcs_group@\fP group to be able to communicate with
the \fIpkcsslotd\fP daemon. Only fully trusted users should be granted
membership in the group. Group members can block other openCryptoki users
from accessing PKCS#11 tokens.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PD 0
